 These properties are accepted in the options object.
 
+##### limit
+
+The maximum number of ranges to take from the header, defaults to no limit.
+Only valid, satisfiable ranges count towards the limit; any ranges after the
+limit is reached are ignored. The limit is applied before `combine`. Values
+that are not a number of at least `1` are ignored.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-1,10-11,20-21', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0,  end: 1 },
+//      { start: 10, end: 11 }
+//    ]
+```
+
